& [AuthorityGrant] is exact
  + future separately claimed CDRA-I01 through CDRA-I07 may implement an effectless in-memory Rust runtime and tests
  + WS-CTPR-011 through WS-CTPR-013 may be reconciled only to compatible bounded slices
  + logical clock, FakeRepository, FakeCalendar, DeterministicPlanner, ChangeCapsule and tandem state machines, compiler fixtures, and replay may be implemented as explicit state transitions
  + no live clock, calendar provider, notification, filesystem, network, database, service, process, thread, Git, model, procedure language, unsafe code, FPGA, device, or external effect
  + current specification campaign performs no implementation

& [Invalidation] is fail-closed
  + any locked artifact hash or byte drift
  + upstream CTPR or pure-form proof invalidation
  + unsupported form used without migration
  + ambient time, nondeterminism, unbounded state, hidden mutable state, or partial admission
  + schedule-as-authority, wake without revalidation, stale join, missing rear evidence, or barrier count substitution
  + compiler fixture generalized beyond its evidence
  + provider, persistence, concurrency, model, hardware, or external effect activation under this signature
  + superseding source or signature protocol change

& [NextBoundary] is explicit
  + CDRA specification work is phase locked
  + a later goal may separately claim CDRA-I01 only, then release dependent slices after proof and completed-work review
  + CPPE and CFLP retain independent signatures and no authority is inherited between them
